{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CLRhP2GtAkJ63nuLmz2G7M","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd036-mktemp\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/mktemp: Create Temporary Files or Directories\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  Shell scripts need unique temporary files and directories for safe intermediate storage.\n6\t  The macOS BSD mktemp uses a different flag set and template convention than GNU mktemp.\n7\t  The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gmktemp, installed by\n8\t  coreutils) on flag behavior, template expansion, and exit codes, verified by differential\n9\t  testing via pkg/testutils. Exact output comparison is not possible because generated names\n10\t  are random; tests must verify structural properties instead.\n11\t\n12\tgoals:\n13\t  - G1: Create a uniquely-named temporary file or directory and print its path to stdout.\n14\t  - G2: Support template customization for the generated name, including suffix and directory placement.\n15\t  - G3: Match GNU mktemp semantics for TMPDIR, -p, --tmpdir, and -t flag interactions.\n16\t\n17\trequirements:\n18\t  R1:\n19\t    title: Default behavior\n20\t    items:\n21\t      - R1.1:\n22\t          text: Must create a temporary file in the directory specified by the TMPDIR environment variable, or /tmp if TMPDIR is unset, and print the absolute path to stdout.\n23\t      - R1.2:\n24\t          text: Must use a template of 'tmp.XXXXXXXXXX' when no template argument is provided, where each X is replaced by a random alphanumeric character.\n25\t      - R1.3:\n26\t          text: When a TEMPLATE argument is provided, must replace the trailing sequence of X characters (minimum three) with random characters and create the file with that name.\n27\t      - R1.4:\n28\t          text: Must create the file with permission mode 0600 (owner read-write only).\n29\t      - R1.5:\n30\t          text: Must exit 0 on success and exit 1 on failure, printing an error to stderr on failure.\n31\t\n32\t  R2:\n33\t    title: Directory mode (-d, --directory)\n34\t    items:\n35\t      - R2.1:\n36\t          text: -d or --directory must create a temporary directory instead of a file.\n37\t      - R2.2:\n38\t          text: Must create the directory with permission mode 0700 (owner read-write-execute only).\n39\t      - R2.3:\n40\t          text: Must print the absolute path of the created directory to stdout.\n41\t\n42\t  R3:\n43\t    title: Template and location control\n44\t    items:\n45\t      - R3.1:\n46\t          text: -p DIR or --tmpdir=DIR must use DIR as the parent directory for the created file or directory, overriding TMPDIR.\n47\t      - R3.2:\n48\t          text: --tmpdir without a value must use TMPDIR or /tmp as the parent directory (same as default behavior), and interpret the next argument as a template.\n49\t      - R3.3:\n50\t          text: --suffix=SUFF must append SUFF after the random characters in the generated name. The template must not contain a slash after the X sequence when --suffix is used.\n51\t      - R3.4:\n52\t          text: -t must treat the template as a filename prefix in the TMPDIR directory, equivalent to legacy BSD compatibility mode in GNU mktemp.\n53\t      - R3.5:\n54\t          text: -u or --dry-run must print the name that would be created without actually creating it, and must print a warning that the option is discouraged.\n55\t      - R3.6:\n56\t          text: -q or --quiet must suppress error messages on failure.\n57\t\n58\t  R4:\n59\t    title: Differential testing\n60\t    items:\n61\t      - R4.1:\n62\t          text: Differential tests must compare exit codes and structural properties of output between the Go binary and gmktemp via pkg/testutils.\n63\t      - R4.2:\n64\t          text: \"Tests must verify structural properties: output is a valid path in the expected directory, the file or directory exists after creation, the name matches the template pattern, and permission bits match the specification.\"\n65\t      - R4.3:\n66\t          text: \"Tests must cover: default file creation, -d directory creation, custom template, --suffix, -p with explicit directory, -t legacy mode, -u dry-run, and error cases for invalid templates.\"\n67\t      - R4.4:\n68\t          text: Tests must not compare exact filenames between the Go binary and gmktemp, since random components will differ between invocations.\n69\t\n70\tnon_goals:\n71\t  - cmd/mktemp does not manage the lifecycle of created files; deletion is the caller's responsibility.\n72\t  - cmd/mktemp does not support creating multiple temporary files in a single invocation.\n73\t  - cmd/mktemp does not read templates from stdin; all input comes from command-line arguments and environment variables.\n74\t\n75\tacceptance_criteria:\n76\t  - id: AC1\n77\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/mktemp creates a file in /tmp matching the pattern tmp.XXXXXXXXXX and prints its path, structurally matching gmktemp output.\"\n78\t    traces:\n79\t      - R1.1\n80\t      - R1.2\n81\t      - R1.3\n82\t      - R1.4\n83\t      - R1.5\n84\t  - id: AC2\n85\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/mktemp -d creates a directory in /tmp with mode 0700, structurally matching gmktemp -d.\"\n86\t    traces:\n87\t      - R2.1\n88\t      - R4.3\n89\t  - id: AC3\n90\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/mktemp -p /var/tmp myapp.XXXX creates a file in /var/tmp matching myapp.XXXX, structurally matching gmktemp -p /var/tmp myapp.XXXX.\"\n91\t    traces:\n92\t      - R3.1\n93\t      - R4.3\n94\t  - id: AC4\n95\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/mktemp --suffix=.txt creates a file ending in .txt, structurally matching gmktemp --suffix=.txt.\"\n96\t    traces:\n97\t      - R3.3\n98\t      - R4.3\n99\t  - id: AC5\n100\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gmktemp passes for structural validation of default, -d, -p, --suffix, -t, and error cases.\"\n101\t    traces:\n102\t      - R1.5\n103\t      - R2.1\n104\t      - R3.1\n105\t      - R3.3\n106\t      - R3.4\n107\t      - R3.6\n108\t      - R4.1\n109\t      - R4.3\n110\t      - R4.4\n111\t  - id: AC6\n112\t    criterion: \"cmd/mktemp compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n113\t    traces:\n114\t      - R1.1\n115\t      - R1.2\n116\t      - R1.3\n117\t      - R1.4\n118\t      - R1.5\n119\t      - R2.1\n120\t      - R2.2\n121\t      - R2.3\n122\t      - R3.1\n123\t      - R3.2\n124\t      - R3.3\n125\t      - R3.4\n126\t      - R3.5\n127\t      - R3.6\n128\t      - R4.1\n129\t      - R4.2\n130\t      - R4.3\n131\t      - R4.4\n132\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7ee43029-eddb-436b-9bcb-30302bda44ca","uuid":"664b0048-4026-414d-a11c-83601c43d948","timestamp":"2026-05-20T12:29:57.278Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5348/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd036-mktemp.yaml","content":"id: srd036-mktemp\ntitle: \"cmd/mktemp: Create Temporary Files or Directories\"\n\nproblem: |\n  Shell scripts need unique temporary files and directories for safe intermediate storage.\n  The macOS BSD mktemp uses a different flag set and template convention than GNU mktemp.\n  The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gmktemp, installed by\n  coreutils) on flag behavior, template expansion, and exit codes, verified by differential\n  testing via pkg/testutils. Exact output comparison is not possible because generated names\n  are random; tests must verify structural properties instead.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Create a uniquely-named temporary file or directory and print its path to stdout.\n  - G2: Support template customization for the generated name, including suffix and directory placement.\n  - G3: Match GNU mktemp semantics for TMPDIR, -p, --tmpdir, and -t flag interactions.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Default behavior\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: Must create a temporary file in the directory specified by the TMPDIR environment variable, or /tmp if TMPDIR is unset, and print the absolute path to stdout.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: Must use a template of 'tmp.XXXXXXXXXX' when no template argument is provided, where each X is replaced by a random alphanumeric character.\n      - R1.3:\n          text: When a TEMPLATE argument is provided, must replace the trailing sequence of X characters (minimum three) with random characters and create the file with that name.\n      - R1.4:\n          text: Must create the file with permission mode 0600 (owner read-write only).\n      - R1.5:\n          text: Must exit 0 on success and exit 1 on failure, printing an error to stderr on failure.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Directory mode (-d, --directory)\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: -d or --directory must create a temporary directory instead of a file.\n      - R2.2:\n          text: Must create the directory with permission mode 0700 (owner read-write-execute only).\n      - R2.3:\n          text: Must print the absolute path of the created directory to stdout.\n\n  R3:\n    title: Template and location control\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: -p DIR or --tmpdir=DIR must use DIR as the parent directory for the created file or directory, overriding TMPDIR.\n      - R3.2:\n          text: --tmpdir without a value must use TMPDIR or /tmp as the parent directory (same as default behavior), and interpret the next argument as a template.\n      - R3.3:\n          text: --suffix=SUFF must append SUFF after the random characters in the generated name. The template must not contain a slash after the X sequence when --suffix is used.\n      - R3.4:\n          text: -t must treat the template as a filename prefix in the TMPDIR directory, equivalent to legacy BSD compatibility mode in GNU mktemp.\n      - R3.5:\n          text: -u or --dry-run must print the name that would be created without actually creating it, and must print a warning that the option is discouraged.\n      - R3.6:\n          text: -q or --quiet must suppress error messages on failure.\n\n  R4:\n    title: Differential testing\n    items:\n      - R4.1:\n          text: Differential tests must compare exit codes and structural properties of output between the Go binary and gmktemp via pkg/testutils.\n      - R4.2:\n          text: \"Tests must verify structural properties: output is a valid path in the expected directory, the file or directory exists after creation, the name matches the template pattern, and permission bits match the specification.\"\n      - R4.3:\n          text: \"Tests must cover: default file creation, -d directory creation, custom template, --suffix, -p with explicit directory, -t legacy mode, -u dry-run, and error cases for invalid templates.\"\n      - R4.4:\n          text: Tests must not compare exact filenames between the Go binary and gmktemp, since random components will differ between invocations.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/mktemp does not manage the lifecycle of created files; deletion is the caller's responsibility.\n  - cmd/mktemp does not support creating multiple temporary files in a single invocation.\n  - cmd/mktemp does not read templates from stdin; all input comes from command-line arguments and environment variables.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/mktemp creates a file in /tmp matching the pattern tmp.XXXXXXXXXX and prints its path, structurally matching gmktemp output.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R1.5\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/mktemp -d creates a directory in /tmp with mode 0700, structurally matching gmktemp -d.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n      - R4.3\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/mktemp -p /var/tmp myapp.XXXX creates a file in /var/tmp matching myapp.XXXX, structurally matching gmktemp -p /var/tmp myapp.XXXX.\"\n    traces:\n      - R3.1\n      - R4.3\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/mktemp --suffix=.txt creates a file ending in .txt, structurally matching gmktemp --suffix=.txt.\"\n    traces:\n      - R3.3\n      - R4.3\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gmktemp passes for structural validation of default, -d, -p, --suffix, -t, and error cases.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.5\n      - R2.1\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.3\n      - R3.4\n      - R3.6\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.3\n      - R4.4\n  - id: AC6\n    criterion: \"cmd/mktemp compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R1.5\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n      - R3.4\n      - R3.5\n      - R3.6\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n      - R4.4\n","numLines":132,"startLine":1,"totalLines":132}}}
